content.text:
I found two places the family can walk into. Brooklyn Children's Museum is left out because its page doesn't say which ages it suits. Both sets of hours come from the venues' own sites. The ticket and date notes below are things the family should know before going.

```json
{
  "picks": [
    {
      "name": "Children's Museum of Manhattan (CMOM), Upper West Side",
      "age_fit": "children ages 0-6",
      "when": "Tuesday-Sunday, 10 am-5 pm",
      "source_name": "Children's Museum of Manhattan"
    },
    {
      "name": "Central Park Zoo (includes the Tisch Children's Zoo)",
      "age_fit": "Child (3 - 12) ticket; Child (2 & under) free",
      "when": "Mon-Fri 10:00am-5:00pm, weekends 10:00am-5:30pm (April 2 - Oct 31, 2026 hours); last entry 1 hour before closing",
      "price": "$16.95 child (3-12), $22.95 adult for Zoo Admission; 2 and under free",
      "source_name": "Central Park Zoo"
    }
  ]
}
```

